          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Our approach</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">How we engaged</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>MEAICON began with a discovery phase across all six participating banks, mapping existing trade-finance workflows, document formats and reconciliation procedures. We identified the common data elements that could be standardized on-chain and the integration points where each bank's core system would connect to the shared ledger.</p>
          <p>From there, we designed the architecture in parallel tracks — the blockchain layer and the security layer — so neither became a bottleneck for the other. Our approach prioritized incremental onboarding so that banks could join the ledger in waves rather than waiting for a single big-bang launch.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Workflow discovery and document standardisation across six banks</li>
            <li>Smart-contract design for trade-document issuance, endorsement and settlement</li>
            <li>Private network segmentation and zero-trust access controls for ledger nodes</li>
            <li>Managed SOC deployment with 24/7 monitoring of ledger and network layer</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
